# Generated xcframework build outputs. build-xcframework.sh regenerates these
# from the Rust sources, and it runs as the FIRST build phase of the "Maple
# Exposure" Xcode target — so the committed copies were overwritten before any
# compile could read them. Tracking them bought nothing and only caused churn:
#
#   * libraw_ffi.a  — Rust static libs, 200-500 MB each (over GitHub's limit).
#   * RawPipeline.h — cbindgen-generated C header (5 copies: one per xcframework
#                     slice + the two include/ dirs). Silently drifted whenever
#                     raw-ffi gained an FFI fn without a header regen (e.g.
#                     maple_histogram_file, #886) and re-diffed across cbindgen
#                     versions.
#
# Both must be rebuilt after a fresh clone anyway (see CLAUDE.md). Bare
# filenames, not a `*.xcframework/**/…` glob (which didn't match on older git).
# Info.plist + module.modulemap stay tracked: static/structural, carry no FFI
# surface (so they don't drift), and keep the xcframework's slice directories
# present at rest so SwiftPM can resolve the .binaryTarget.
libraw_ffi.a
RawPipeline.h

